## Summary
An iconic fast-food fried chicken chain is closing over 300 restaurants amid declining performance. The brand has struggled to compete against rapidly growing rivals such as Chick-fil-A and Raising Cane's.

## Key Points
- An iconic fast-food fried chicken chain is shutting down more than 300 restaurant locations
- The closures reflect broader struggles for legacy fast-food brands in the competitive chicken segment
- Upstart rivals Chick-fil-A and Raising Cane's are gaining market share at the expense of established chains
- The fast-food fried chicken market has become increasingly competitive in recent years


